---
id: org.dxos.plugin.code
name: CodePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

```mdl
plugin CodePlugin: Authors, reviews and syncs DEUS specs, and scaffolds the code they describe.
  id: org.dxos.plugin.code
  dependsOn: [org.dxos.plugin.projects]
  modules:
    - AppGraphBuilder: graph nodes for specs and code projects
    - BuildRunState: the state of the running build agent, from CodeEvents.Start
    - CreateObject: create entries for SpecDocument and CodeProject
    - NavigationTargetResolver: resolves a github: key to the spec or file it names
    - OperationHandler: the plugin's operations (importSpec, listLocalSpecs, the Coder tools)
    - PluginAsset: this document, served as the plugin's own spec
    - ReactSurface: the spec article surface, and the code project's article and section surfaces
    - Schema: the SpecDocument and CodeProject types
    - Settings: repos to sync and build settings
    - SkillDefinition: the Coder skill
    - SpecFileMapping: the GitHubCapabilities.FileMapping for `**/*.mdl`, so a GitHub file binding syncs specs (org.dxos.plugin.github.file-sync#F-6)
    - SpecSync: two-way sync of specs with files on disk (plugin-file-system's FileSystem)
    - Translations: the plugin's strings
```

A plugin for AI-assisted Composer plugin development. Hosts authored DEUS specs
(`.mdl` files), couples them to a `CodeProject`, and provides a Coder skill
that lets the assistant verify a spec, write source files into the project,
and (eventually) dispatch a build agent. The build/sandbox itself is a
separate EDGE service (out of scope until phase 2).

Phase 1 shipped: rename, schema, skill scaffold, settings, credential
wiring, and stub `verifySpec` / `runBuildAgent` operations.

Phase 1.5 (this PR) adds an in-memory CRUD surface for source files. The agent
can scaffold a project, list/read/write/delete files, and call the
`introspect-mcp` server to look up DXOS / Composer APIs. All file state is
ECHO-canonical — there is no sandbox or build runtime yet. The CodeArticle
renders a file tree alongside a CodeMirror editor (via `react-ui-editor`'s
`Editor.Root`) so a human can see what the agent is producing.

The plugin reuses `react-ui-editor`'s `Editor.Root` / `Editor.Toolbar` /
`Editor.Content` together with the existing `mdl()` CodeMirror extensions
instead of a bespoke editor implementation.

## Dependencies

```mdl
uses org.dxos.echo: Spec and CodeProject are ECHO objects, read and written through its Database.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem: Its FileSystem service is the only way spec sync reaches local files.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.devShell: Its dev-only `bash` route is the pattern the sync dev route follows.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.plugin.github.file-sync: Its FileMapping contract, which the `.mdl` mapping implements.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.spec.review: The review dialect whose verdicts the spec viewer reads and marks.
```

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`    |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |
| `question`  | `org.dxos.mdl.question@1.0`   |
| `plugin`    | `org.dxos.mdl.plugin@1.0`     |
| `uses`      | `dxos.spec.core/uses`         |

## Types

```mdl
type SpecDocument
  desc: |
    A DEUS spec document. Carries `.mdl` content and a human-readable name.
    Typename `org.dxos.type.specDocument`; objects stored as `org.dxos.type.spec` migrate to it.
  fields:
    name?: string
    content: Ref<Text>          # mdl source
```

```mdl
type CodeProject
  desc: |
    A coding project. Pairs a name with a SpecDocument used to drive code generation
    and the set of TypeScript source files that compose the plugin.
    Typename `org.dxos.type.codeProject`.
  fields:
    name?: string
    spec: Ref<SpecDocument>     # the DEUS spec authored for this project
    files?: Ref<SourceFile>[]   # source tree, hierarchy implicit in path
```

```mdl
type SourceFile
  desc: |
    A single file in a CodeProject. The path is POSIX-style with folder
    separators ("src/components/Button.tsx"); folder objects are not modeled
    explicitly. `content` references a Text object so edits flow through ECHO
    reactivity and CRDT conflict resolution.
    Typename `org.dxos.type.sourceFile`.
  fields:
    path: string                # e.g. "src/plugin.ts"
    content: Ref<Text>
    mode?: number               # POSIX file mode; reserved for future use
```

```mdl
type Settings
  desc: |
    Plugin settings (plugin-scoped, not per-space). Reactive.
    The Anthropic API key itself is NOT stored here — it lives in an
    AccessToken ECHO object with source `anthropic.com`, accessed via
    the composer credentials API.
  fields:
    endpoint?: string           # URL of the EDGE build service (phase-2 wiring)
    repos?: string[]            # local checkouts for spec sync (F-14.2)
```

## Components

```mdl
component CodeArticle
  desc: |
    Article surface for a CodeProject. Two-pane layout: the left pane is a
    FileTree built from `project.files`, the right pane is a `react-ui-editor`
    `Editor.Root` bound to the selected SourceFile's `content` Text. Selecting
    a file in the tree replaces the editor's extensions to pick up the right
    language (`javascript({ typescript: true })` for .ts/.tsx, `markdown()`
    for .md, plain text otherwise). Edits flow through `createDataExtensions`
    so the underlying ECHO Text is updated reactively.
  props:
    role: string
    subject: CodeProject
    attendableId?: string
  state:
    selectedPath?: string
  layout: |
    ┌──────────────┬──────────────────────────┐
    │ FileTree     │ Editor.View              │
    │  package.json│   (lang based on path)   │
    │  ▾ src/      │                          │
    │    plugin.ts │                          │
    │  README.md   │                          │
    └──────────────┴──────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component FileTree
  desc: |
    Renders a flat list of SourceFile-style entries as a hierarchical tree.
    Folders are derived from path components and rendered as collapsible
    nodes; clicking a leaf calls `onSelect`. Pure component — no ECHO
    awareness — to keep storybook coverage simple.
  props:
    files: { path: string }[]
    selectedPath?: string
    onSelect?: (path: string) => void
    emptyMessage?: string
```

```mdl
component SpecArticle
  desc: |
    Article surface for a SpecDocument, laid out as an IDE page: the MDL editor beside a
    panel of views (definitions graph, review, code, decisions by person, decision graph,
    data model, API).
    Uses `react-ui-editor`'s Editor primitives with the `mdl()` extensions.
    Source keys to other specs are links (F-15); the latest review marks each
    reviewed item and links it to its code (F-16). Extensions plugin-projects
    contributes (`ProjectCapabilities.SpecDocumentExtensions`), such as feature
    cards for the objects the text embeds, are added to the editor.
  props:
    role: string
    subject?: SpecDocument
    content?: string            # static text, e.g. a bundled PLUGIN.mdl
    sourceKey?: string          # github: key of static content
    attendableId?: string
  state:
    view: definitions | review | code | log | decisions | data | api
    codeTarget?: string         # the github: key open in the code view
  layout: |
    ┌──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┐
    │ key · sync status        │ [Defs|Review|Code|…]         │
    ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
    │ ```mdl   [</> make][Done]│  ┌─────┐   ┌ ─ ─ ─ ┐         │
    │ feat F-1: …   [Missing]  │  │ F-1 │──▶  Database        │
    │  org.dxos.echo#Database  │  └─────┘   └ ─ ─ ─ ┘         │
    └──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component CodeSettings
  desc: |
    Settings surface contributed via `AppPlugin.addSettingsModule`. Lets the
    user paste/clear an Anthropic API key. The key is persisted to an
    AccessToken (source `anthropic.com`) in the user's HALO space; reads/
    writes go through the composer credentials API, not Settings.
  props:
    settings: Settings
  state:
    apiKey?: string             # bound to AccessToken.token
  actions:
    saveApiKey(value: string)
    clearApiKey()
```

## Services

```mdl
service Credentials
  desc: |
    Composer credentials API (`@dxos/functions/services/CredentialsService`).
    Used by `CodeSettings` to read/write the Anthropic API key as an
    AccessToken with source `anthropic.com`.
  ops:
    getCredential(query: { service: string }) → ServiceCredential
    queryCredentials(query: { service: string }) → ServiceCredential[]
```

```mdl
service BuildAgent
  desc: |
    The remote EDGE service that runs the Claude Agent SDK to generate
    Composer plugins from a SpecDocument. Out of scope for this PR — phase 1 only
    declares the contract surface. Will live in `dxos/edge`.
  loading: lazy
  ops:
    verify(spec: SpecDocument) → { ok: bool, messages: string[] }
    build(project: CodeProject) → { runId: string, status: string }
```

## Operations

Phase-1 ops (`verifySpec`, `runBuildAgent`) are stubs until the EDGE build
service exists. Phase-1.5 adds real handlers for file CRUD over ECHO; no
sandbox is involved.

```mdl
op verifySpec
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.verifySpec
  desc: |
    Static verification of a DEUS spec — lint + structural checks. Phase-1
    stub returns `{ ok: true, messages: [] }`. Will eventually delegate to
    BuildAgent.verify.
  input:
    spec: Ref<SpecDocument>
  output: { ok: bool, messages: string[] }
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database]
  note: |
    Operation key: `org.dxos.operation.code.verifySpec`.
    Exposed as a skill tool on CoderSkill.
```

```mdl
op runBuildAgent
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.runBuildAgent
  desc: |
    Dispatches a build of the project via the EDGE BuildAgent. Phase-1 stub
    returns `{ status: "queued" }` without performing any work.
  input:
    project: Ref<CodeProject>
  output: { status: queued | running | succeeded | failed }
  effects: [echo:read, http]
  requires: [Database, Credentials]
  note: |
    Operation key: `org.dxos.operation.code.runBuildAgent`.
    Phase-2: reads the Anthropic API key via Credentials and POSTs to the
    EDGE BuildAgent endpoint configured in Settings.endpoint.
```

```mdl
op listFiles
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.listFiles
  desc: List the source files in a CodeProject (path + size).
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject> }
  output: { files: { path: string, size: number }[] }   # sorted ascending by path
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.listFiles`.
```

```mdl
op readFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.readFile
  desc: Read the content of a single file in a CodeProject.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject>, path: string }
  output: { path: string, content: string }
  errors: [FileNotFound]
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.readFile`.
```

```mdl
op writeFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.writeFile
  desc: |
    Create or overwrite a file in a CodeProject. Whole-file write — for
    targeted edits, prefer reading first and writing back the new content.
    Returns `created: true` for new files, `created: false` for overwrites.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject>, path: string, content: string }
  output: { path: string, created: boolean }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.writeFile`.
```

```mdl
op deleteFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.deleteFile
  desc: Remove a file from a CodeProject by path.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject>, path: string }
  output: { path: string, deleted: boolean }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.deleteFile`.
```

```mdl
op scaffoldProject
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.scaffold
  desc: |
    Seed a CodeProject with a minimal Composer plugin scaffold
    (package.json, src/plugin.ts, README.md). Idempotent — overwrites any
    files at the scaffold paths but never deletes user files.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject>, name?: string }
  output: { files: { path: string, size: number }[] }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.scaffold`.
```

```mdl
op helloWorld
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.writeHelloWorld
  desc: |
    Sanity-check operation. Writes (or overwrites) a single `src/hello.ts`
    file containing a Hello World program. Used to verify end-to-end that
    the agent can manipulate the file abstraction and that the result
    surfaces in the CodeArticle.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject> }
  output: { path: string, created: boolean }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.writeHelloWorld`.
```

```mdl
op resetProject
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.reset
  desc: |
    Delete every source file in a CodeProject. Destructive; intended for
    testing and iteration when the agent needs a clean slate. Removes
    each SourceFile (and its owned Text) from ECHO and clears the
    project's `files` array.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject> }
  output: { removed: number }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.reset`.
```

```mdl
op buildProject
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.buildProject
  desc: |
    Compile the project's TypeScript sources in-browser. F-12a transpiles a
    single entry file (`src/hello.ts` if present, else `src/plugin.ts`) with
    the TypeScript language service (no bundling, no imports). F-12b
    extends to multi-file bundling via esbuild-wasm with the project's
    SourceFiles as a virtual filesystem. Returns diagnostics from the TS
    language service and the emitted JS for the entry. Distinct from
    `runBuildAgent`, which targets the remote EDGE codegen service.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject> }
  output: {
    ok: bool,
    diagnostics: { path?: string, line?: number, column?: number, severity: "error" | "warning", code?: number, message: string }[],
    entry?: { path: string, source: string }
  }
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.buildProject`.
```

```mdl
op runBuild
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.runBuild
  desc: |
    Build the project and, on a clean build, execute the entry source on the
    main thread inside a `console`-capturing wrapper. Captures `console.log`
    / `console.warn` (→ stdout) and `console.error` plus uncaught errors
    (→ stderr). Synchronous-only in F-12a; the wrapper restores the original
    console even on throw.
  input:  { project: Ref<CodeProject> }
  output: {
    ok: bool,
    stdout: string[],
    stderr: string[],
    diagnostics: { path?: string, line?: number, column?: number, severity: "error" | "warning", code?: number, message: string }[]
  }
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database]
  note:   Operation key `org.dxos.operation.code.runBuild`.
```

```mdl
op importSpec
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.importSpec
  desc: |
    Links a spec file in a local checkout to a SpecDocument, keyed by its source key;
    returns the existing SpecDocument when one already carries the key (F-14.6).
  input:
    key: string                 # github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>.mdl
  output: { spec: Ref<SpecDocument>, created: boolean }
  errors:
    - CodeOperationError: not a spec key, no checkout of the repository, or no such file
  effects: [fs, echo:write]
  requires: [org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem#FileSystem]
```

```mdl
op importSpecFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.importSpecFile
  desc: |
    The import of the `.mdl` FileMapping: creates a SpecDocument for a new file, or applies the remote
    change to SpecDocument.content with TextMerge.applyAt as of the heads of the last sync.
  input: FileImportInput        # org.dxos.plugin.github.file-sync#FileMapping
  output: FileImportOutput
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
```

```mdl
op exportSpecFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.exportSpecFile
  desc: The export of the `.mdl` FileMapping: SpecDocument.content as it stands, with the heads it was read at.
  input: FileExportInput
  output: FileExportOutput
  effects: [echo:read]
```

```mdl
op listLocalSpecs
  key: org.dxos.operation.code.listLocalSpecs
  desc: Lists the `.mdl` specs in every known checkout as source keys, reviews excluded.
  input:
    (none)
  output: { roots: { repo: string, path: string }[], keys: string[] }
  effects: [fs]
  requires: [org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem#FileSystem]
```

## Skills

```mdl
type CoderSkill
  desc: |
    Skill key `org.dxos.skill.coder`. Drives plugin authoring:
    iterate on the Spec with the user, look up DXOS / Composer APIs through
    introspect-mcp, scaffold the project, then write/read/delete source
    files until the user is satisfied.
  fields:
    key: org.dxos.skill.coder
    tools:
      - op:verifySpec
      - op:runBuildAgent
      - op:listFiles
      - op:readFile
      - op:writeFile
      - op:deleteFile
      - op:scaffoldProject
      - op:helloWorld
      - op:resetProject
      - op:buildProject
      - op:runBuild
    # The introspect-mcp tools (list_packages, get_package, list_symbols,
    # find_symbol, get_symbol) come from the built-in DXOS Introspect MCP
    # server (org.dxos.mcp.introspect), off in a chat until turned on.
    instructions: prose
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Rename plugin-spec → plugin-code

  req F-1.1: Package renamed `@dxos/plugin-spec` → `@dxos/plugin-code`.
  req F-1.2: Directory renamed `packages/plugins/plugin-spec` → `packages/plugins/plugin-code`.
  req F-1.3: Plugin id renamed `org.dxos.plugin.spec` → `org.dxos.plugin.code`.
  req F-1.4: SpecPlugin → CodePlugin; SpecArticle → CodeArticle.
  req F-1.5: The spec document type keeps its data across renames: objects stored as `org.dxos.type.spec` migrate to
    `org.dxos.type.specDocument`.
  req F-1.6:
    when: composer-app loads after rename
    then: existing spec documents continue to render
```

```mdl
feat F-2: CodeProject type

  req F-2.1: New ECHO type `CodeProject` with typename `org.dxos.type.codeProject`.
  req F-2.2: Fields `name?: string`, `spec: Ref<SpecDocument>`; both reactive.
  req F-2.3:
    when: user creates a CodeProject from the navtree
    then: an empty Spec is created and referenced by the new CodeProject
  req F-2.4: CodeProject registered via `addSchemaModule` and `addMetadataModule`.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: CodeArticle uses react-ui-editor

  req F-3.1: CodeArticle uses `Editor.Root` + `Editor.Toolbar` + `Editor.Content`
             from `@dxos/react-ui-editor` instead of a bespoke `useTextEditor` setup.
  req F-3.2: The existing `mdl()`, `mdlBlockDescription`, `mdlLint`, `mdlComplete`
             extensions are passed to the editor.
  req F-3.3:
    when: a Spec is opened
    then: its `content` is editable with markdown + .mdl block highlighting
  req F-3.4: Toolbar exposes a Spec | Code tab toggle via `customActions`.
  req F-3.5:
    when: user clicks "Code"
    then: editor area is hidden and a placeholder ("Build output will appear here") is shown
  req F-3.6:
    when: user clicks "Spec"
    then: editor area is restored and focus returns to the document
  req F-3.7: Active tab is local component state (not persisted).
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Settings + credentials

  req F-4.1: `Settings` schema mutable, with optional `endpoint: string`.
  req F-4.2: Settings registered via `AppPlugin.addSettingsModule`.
  req F-4.3: A `CodeSettings` container renders an API-key input.
  req F-4.4:
    when: user enters an API key and saves
    then: an `AccessToken` is upserted with `source: "anthropic.com"`, `token: <value>`
          via the composer credentials API
  req F-4.5:
    when: user clears the key
    then: the matching AccessToken is removed
  req F-4.6: API key value is never stored in `Settings`.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Coder skill

  req F-5.1: A skill with key `org.dxos.skill.coder` is contributed
             via `addSkillDefinitionModule`.
  req F-5.2: Tools include op:verifySpec and op:runBuildAgent.
  req F-5.3: System instructions describe the Coder role:
              author/refine spec with user, run verifySpec, then runBuildAgent.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Stub operations

  req F-6.1: op:verifySpec defined and handler returns `{ ok: true, messages: [] }`.
  req F-6.2: op:runBuildAgent defined and handler returns `{ status: "queued" }`.
  req F-6.3: Both handlers are contributed via `addOperationHandlerModule`.
  req F-6.4: Both operations resolve from skill tool calls without error.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Source files in ECHO

  req F-7.1: New ECHO type SourceFile with typename `org.dxos.type.sourceFile`.
  req F-7.2: CodeProject extended with optional `files: Ref<SourceFile>[]`.
  req F-7.3: SourceFile registered via `addSchemaModule` and translations.
  req F-7.4:
    when: a SourceFile is mutated through write-file
    then: the underlying Text object is updated; the file Ref already in
          `project.files` is reused (no duplicate file objects per path).
  req F-7.5:
    when: a path that doesn't yet exist is written
    then: a new SourceFile + Text are created and appended to `project.files`.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: File CRUD operations

  req F-8.1: op:listFiles returns the project's files sorted by path.
  req F-8.2: op:readFile resolves a file by exact-path match and returns its content.
  req F-8.3:
    when: op:readFile is called with an unknown path
    then: the operation fails with a FileNotFound error
  req F-8.4: op:writeFile creates new files and overwrites existing ones (whole-file).
  req F-8.5: op:deleteFile removes the matching file from `project.files`.
  req F-8.6: op:scaffoldProject seeds package.json, src/plugin.ts, README.md and
             returns the resulting file list.
  req F-8.7: All file ops are wired into the CoderSkill tool set.
```

```mdl
feat F-9: CodeArticle file tree + editor

  req F-9.1: CodeArticle renders a two-pane layout: FileTree on the left,
             editor on the right.
  req F-9.2: FileTree is a pure component (no ECHO awareness) and is unit-
             coverable from a Storybook story.
  req F-9.3: Selecting a file replaces the editor's language extension based
             on the file's extension (`.ts`/`.tsx` → typescript JS, `.md` →
             markdown, otherwise plain JS).
  req F-9.4: The editor is `react-ui-editor`'s `Editor.Root` with
             `createDataExtensions` so edits propagate back into the
             SourceFile's Text via ECHO.
  req F-9.5:
    when: the agent writes a new file via op:writeFile
    then: the file appears in the FileTree on the next render
  req F-9.6:
    when: `project.files` is empty
    then: an empty-state message points the user at the Coder agent
```

```mdl
feat F-10: Coder integrates introspect-mcp

  req F-10.1: CoderSkill declares a remote MCP server entry pointing at the
              introspect-mcp HTTP endpoint.
  req F-10.2: System prompt directs the agent to call introspect-mcp
              (find_symbol / get_symbol / list_packages …) before writing
              code that touches DXOS / Composer APIs.
  req F-10.3:
    when: introspect-mcp is unreachable
    then: chat continues to function (per @dxos/plugin-assistant resilience);
          the agent simply has no API search tools available.
```

```mdl
feat F-11: Sanity + reset operations

  req F-11.1: op:helloWorld writes (or overwrites) `src/hello.ts` containing a
              minimal Hello World program; idempotent.
  req F-11.2: op:resetProject removes every SourceFile from `project.files`
              and calls Database.remove + flush so the underlying ECHO
              objects are not leaked.
  req F-11.3: Both operations are wired into the CoderSkill tool set.
  req F-11.4:
    when: the user asks the agent to "build hello world"
    then: the agent invokes op:helloWorld and `src/hello.ts` shows up in the
          FileTree on the next render.
  req F-11.5:
    when: the user asks the agent to "reset the project"
    then: the agent invokes op:resetProject and the FileTree shows the
          empty-state placeholder.
```

```mdl
feat F-12a: Local build & run — single-file entry

  req F-12a.1: A `Compiler` module wraps `@typescript/vfs`'s virtual TS
               environment. lib.d.ts files are fetched lazily from the
               TypeScript playground CDN on first use and cached for the
               lifetime of the page. The compiler instance is module-level
               and reused across operation invocations.
  req F-12a.2: op:buildProject identifies an entry file (`src/hello.ts` if
               present, else `src/plugin.ts`), feeds its content to the
               compiler, and returns the language service's syntactic +
               semantic diagnostics plus the emitted JS for the entry.
  req F-12a.3:
    when: op:buildProject is called and no entry file exists
    then: it returns `{ ok: false, diagnostics: [...], entry: undefined }`
          with a diagnostic explaining the entry is missing
  req F-12a.4: op:runBuild internally builds the project; on a clean build
               it evaluates the emitted JS via `new Function(...)` inside a
               wrapper that captures `console.log` / `console.warn` (→ stdout)
               and `console.error` plus thrown errors (→ stderr).
  req F-12a.5: The console-capture wrapper restores `console` even on throw,
               and never leaks captured strings between concurrent calls
               (each call uses its own arrays + per-call console shim).
  req F-12a.6:
    when: the entry source throws at runtime
    then: op:runBuild returns `{ ok: false, stdout, stderr: [...err], diagnostics: [] }`
          and does not throw
  req F-12a.7: Both ops are registered in the OperationHandlerSet and added
               to CoderSkill's tool set. The Coder system prompt mentions
               `build-project` and `run-build` and the recommended sequence
               (write source → build → run).
  req F-12a.8: The CodeArticle toolbar exposes Build and Run buttons. Run is
               disabled until the most recent build for the current project
               completed cleanly. The bottom-left inspect-pane TODO is
               replaced with a Diagnostics / Console pane showing the last
               build's diagnostics and the last run's stdout/stderr.
  req F-12a.9: Per-project build/run state lives in a CodePlugin capability
               atom keyed by `CodeProject.id`. CodeArticle reads the atom for
               the open project; remounting the article does not lose state.
```

```mdl
feat F-12b: Local build & run — multi-file bundling

  req F-12b.1: `esbuild-wasm` is added as a workspace catalog dependency.
               Esbuild is initialized lazily on first multi-file build; the
               WASM binary loads from the npm package URL and is cached by
               the browser.
  req F-12b.2: A `bundle(files, entryPath)` helper wraps esbuild with a
               custom plugin that resolves bare and relative paths against
               the in-memory SourceFile set. Paths the plugin cannot resolve
               within the project surface as esbuild diagnostics.
  req F-12b.3: op:buildProject chooses a strategy: if the project has
               exactly one `.ts`/`.tsx` file and that file has no imports,
               it uses the plain TS transpile path (F-12a); otherwise it
               uses esbuild for bundling, with the TS language service still
               providing type-check diagnostics.
  req F-12b.4:
    when: op:buildProject runs on a project with `src/util.ts` and
          `src/hello.ts` (where `hello.ts` imports from `./util`)
    then: the build returns one bundled `entry.source` containing both
          modules, the bundle executes via op:runBuild, and stdout reflects
          values defined in `util.ts`
  req F-12b.5: External imports (anything not matching a path in the
               project's SourceFiles) are treated as build errors in
               F-12b. Host-externals via import maps are deferred to F-13.
```

```mdl
feat F-14: Two-way spec sync with a local checkout
  desc: |
    A Spec can be linked to a `.mdl` file in a git checkout by source key
    (`github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>`), stored in its meta keys in the shape
    plugin-projects already writes ({ source: github.com/<owner>/<repo>, id: <path> }).
    Linked specs sync both ways while the app runs, so Composer is the viewer
    for specs that live in the repository.

  req F-14.1: Sync reaches local files only through plugin-file-system's
              org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem#FileSystem service: the
              Tauri fs plugin in the desktop app, and a dev-only route in a
              Composer dev server, the same pattern as
              org.dxos.plugin.devShell#bash.
              Sync writes only `.mdl` files; a deployed web app has neither
              backend and leaves sync off.
  req F-14.2: A key's repository resolves to a checkout from the `repos` setting
              (an absolute path whose GitHub remote names the repo, or
              `owner/repo=/abs/path`), then from the dev server's own working tree.
  req F-14.3: Every 2 seconds each linked Spec is reconciled three-way against the
              last text both sides agreed on: a change on one side flows to the
              other; with no base, or when both changed, the file wins.
  req F-14.4: A pull applies a minimal text diff, so open editors keep their
              cursors.
  req F-14.5: The dev route reads files only inside its roots (the workspace and
              `DX_FS_ROOTS`) and writes only `.mdl` files.
  req F-14.6: op:importSpec links a file to a new Spec, or returns the Spec that
              already carries the key.
  req F-14.7: A document a plugin-projects spec holds syncs through
              `ProjectCapabilities.SpecDocumentCodec`: a push writes the codec's text for
              it, made against the last synced text, and a pull hands the file to the
              codec. Any other document's text is copied as it is.
```

```mdl
feat F-15: Source-key references to other specs
  desc: |
    A spec names a block of another spec by the spec's id and the block's id, e.g.
    org.dxos.echo#Database. Links to the code
    that implements a spec are not spec text; they are annotations (F-16.5).

  req F-15.1: The definitions graph draws each named external block as a dashed
              box with an edge from the block that names it, described from the
              other spec's text when its checkout is known.
  req F-15.2: Ctrl/⌘-click on a key in the editor, or double-click on an external
              box, opens the other spec as its own synced Spec.
  req F-15.3: The Code view shows a source file at a symbol's declaration line,
              and opens the file in VS Code where the host knows its local path.
```

```mdl
feat F-16: Compliance review annotations
  desc: |
    The `spec-review` skill writes `<SPEC>.review.mdl` beside a spec: one verdict
    per item, in the review dialect (`org.dxos.spec.review`).

  req F-16.1: SpecArticle reads the review beside the spec from the checkout and
              re-reads it every 3 seconds.
  req F-16.2: Each reviewed item's declaration line gets a status bar and chip in
              the margin; a chip opens the verdict in the Review view.
  req F-16.3: Each definitions-graph box gets a status badge; a feature shows the
              worst status of its requirements.
  req F-16.4: The Review view lists verdicts worst first as cards in a list: each
              card shows its status icon and item id, with a menu top right that
              shows the item in the spec or opens its code; the current card
              follows the item selected in the spec.
  req F-16.5: A verdict's evidence keys are the spec's links to its code: each
              reviewed item's declaration line gets a chip per symbol in the
              margin, beside the decision chips, and the definitions graph draws
              the symbols as dashed code boxes. A chip click or a box double-click
              opens the Code view at the symbol.
  req F-16.6: Each `scenario` and `test` is reviewed for whether automation exercises
              it: its declaration line shows tested, partly tested or not tested,
              with a chip per test file that opens the test's code.
  req F-16.7: Hovering a code or test chip shows a card with the file name and the
              declaration of the named symbol, read from the checkout; a key with no
              symbol shows the file's first lines. A click still opens the Code view.
  req F-16.8: An item with more than one implementation, or with a `walkthrough:` in its
              verdict, has a walkthrough: 1 to 5 segments, each one sentence and a code
              snippet that links to its file. It shows inline in the item's card in the
              Review view, and in a card when the status chip is hovered. An item with
              one implementation has no walkthrough; the chip's hover card is enough.
```

```mdl
feat F-17: Diff mode
  desc: |
    Reviewing a spec on a branch means reading what changed since the branch's base, in the text
    and in the definitions graph.

  req F-17.1: SpecArticle shows the checkout's branch, or its open pull request as a
              link, and offers diff mode against the pull request's base (else the
              default branch) at the commit the branch forked from, or against HEAD.
  req F-17.2: In diff mode the editor shows removed lines in place, faded and struck
              through, and new lines tinted; unchanged runs can be folded.
  req F-17.3: In diff mode the definitions graph also draws what the base had: new
              definitions and arrows green, changed definitions amber, removed ones
              faded and dashed, with counts in the legend.
  req F-17.4: Git is read through the FileSystem service's read-only `git` queries
              (status, file at a commit), which the dev route answers.
```

```mdl
feat F-18: Spec questions
  desc: |
    A `question` in a spec's changelog is a choice nobody has made yet. It is answered in
    Composer, and the answer is recorded as a decision.

  req F-18.1: SpecArticle has a decisions-by-person view: the changelog's decisions grouped by
              decider, with the spec's questions above them, open ones first.
  req F-18.2: Each question is drawn with the question component the chat uses: its context,
              its options, and a free-form answer field.
  req F-18.3: In an editable spec, an answer appends to `## Changelog` a decision by the person
              who answered, with `answers:` naming the question. A read-only spec lists its
              questions without the answer controls.
  req F-18.4: The decision graph draws each question as a card, with an edge to the decision
              that answers it. A question's `affects:` puts a chip on each block it names, and the
              chip opens the decisions-by-person view.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Rename preserves Spec compatibility
  given: a space already containing a Spec object created by plugin-spec
  when: the renamed plugin-code is loaded
  then:
    - the object is queryable as a SpecDocument
    - opening it renders CodeArticle with the same content
    - its typename is `org.dxos.type.specDocument`
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Create CodeProject
  given: composer-app with plugin-code loaded
  when: user invokes "Create CodeProject" from a space
  then:
    - a new CodeProject object is created with default name
    - a new empty Spec is created and referenced via `project.spec`
    - opening the project surfaces the linked Spec via CodeArticle
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Editor renders mdl content
  given: a Spec containing an mdl fenced block
  when: CodeArticle mounts
  then:
    - markdown is decorated by `decorateMarkdown()`
    - the mdl block body is highlighted by `mdlBlockDescription`
    - lint and completion sources are wired
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Toolbar tab toggle
  given: a CodeArticle is open showing the Spec view
  when: user clicks the Code tab
  then:
    - the editor content is hidden
    - the Code placeholder ("Build output will appear here") is visible
  when: user clicks the Spec tab
  then: the editor content is visible again
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Save API key persists AccessToken
  given: CodeSettings is open and no AccessToken exists for `anthropic.com`
  when: user enters a key and clicks save
  then:
    - an AccessToken with `source: "anthropic.com"` and the entered token is created
    - the input shows the masked persisted value on next render
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: Clear API key removes AccessToken
  given: an AccessToken exists for `anthropic.com`
  when: user clicks clear
  then:
    - the AccessToken is removed
    - subsequent `CredentialsService.getCredential({ service: "anthropic.com" })` rejects
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: Skill registers tools
  given: composer-app with plugin-code loaded
  when: AppCapabilities.SkillDefinition is queried for `org.dxos.skill.coder`
  then:
    - the skill is present
    - its tool set includes verifySpec and runBuildAgent
```

```mdl
scenario T-8: Stub operations resolve
  given: an assistant chat with the Coder skill loaded
  when: the assistant invokes verifySpec on a Spec
  then: the call returns `{ ok: true, messages: [] }`
  when: the assistant invokes runBuildAgent on a CodeProject
  then: the call returns `{ status: "queued" }`
```

```mdl
scenario T-9: Scaffold seeds project files
  given: an empty CodeProject
  when: op:scaffoldProject is invoked with name "demo"
  then:
    - `project.files` includes SourceFiles at paths package.json, src/plugin.ts, README.md
    - each file's Text content is non-empty and reflects the project name
```

```mdl
scenario T-10: Round-trip read/write/delete
  given: a CodeProject with one file at "src/foo.ts"
  when: op:writeFile is called with path "src/foo.ts" and content "X"
  then: op:writeFile returns `created: false`; op:readFile returns content "X"
  when: op:writeFile is called with path "src/bar.ts" and content "Y"
  then: op:writeFile returns `created: true`; op:readFile returns content "Y"
  when: op:deleteFile is called with path "src/bar.ts"
  then: op:listFiles no longer reports "src/bar.ts"
```

```mdl
scenario T-11: CodeArticle reflects ECHO mutations
  given: a CodeArticle is mounted on a CodeProject
  when: a new SourceFile is added to `project.files` via op:writeFile
  then: the FileTree shows the new path on next render without manual reload
```

```mdl
scenario T-12: Coder skill exposes file tools
  given: composer-app with plugin-code loaded
  when: AppCapabilities.SkillDefinition is queried for `org.dxos.skill.coder`
  then:
    - the skill's tool set includes listFiles, readFile, writeFile,
      deleteFile, scaffoldProject, helloWorld, and resetProject
    - the skill declares an introspect-mcp remote MCP server
```

```mdl
scenario T-13: Hello World sanity round-trip
  given: a CodeProject with no files
  when: op:helloWorld is invoked
  then:
    - `project.files` includes exactly one SourceFile at path "src/hello.ts"
    - the result is `{ path: "src/hello.ts", created: true }`
  when: op:helloWorld is invoked a second time
  then: the result is `{ path: "src/hello.ts", created: false }` and the
        file count is unchanged (idempotent overwrite)
```

```mdl
scenario T-14: Reset clears project files
  given: a CodeProject with N (>0) files
  when: op:resetProject is invoked
  then:
    - the result is `{ removed: N }`
    - `project.files` is empty
    - each previously-referenced SourceFile has been removed from ECHO
      (`Database.remove` + flush)
  when: op:resetProject is invoked on an already-empty project
  then: the result is `{ removed: 0 }`
```

```mdl
scenario T-15: Build the Hello World scaffold
  given: a CodeProject with `src/hello.ts` containing the helloWorld scaffold
  when: op:buildProject is invoked
  then:
    - the result is `{ ok: true, diagnostics: [], entry: { path: "src/hello.ts", source: <non-empty JS> } }`
    - `entry.source` is a transpiled JavaScript string (no remaining `:` type
      annotations on declarations)
  given: a CodeProject whose only file is `src/hello.ts` with a syntax error
  when: op:buildProject is invoked
  then: the result is `{ ok: false, diagnostics: [{severity: "error", ...}] }`
        and `entry` is undefined
```

```mdl
scenario T-16: Run the Hello World scaffold
  given: a CodeProject containing only the helloWorld scaffold
  when: op:runBuild is invoked
  then:
    - the result is `{ ok: true, stdout: [..., "Hello, World!"], stderr: [], diagnostics: [] }`
  given: a CodeProject whose entry throws at runtime
  when: op:runBuild is invoked
  then: the result is `{ ok: false, stdout: [...], stderr: [<error message>], diagnostics: [] }`
        and the operation does not raise
```

```mdl
scenario T-17: Coder skill exposes build/run tools
  given: composer-app with plugin-code loaded
  when: AppCapabilities.SkillDefinition is queried for `org.dxos.skill.coder`
  then: the skill's tool set includes buildProject and runBuild
```

```mdl
scenario T-18: Multi-file bundle round-trip (F-12b)
  given: a CodeProject with two files:
         - src/util.ts: `export const MESSAGE = "from util";`
         - src/hello.ts: `import { MESSAGE } from "./util"; console.log(MESSAGE);`
  when: op:buildProject is invoked
  then: the build is clean and `entry.source` includes the bundled contents of util.ts
  when: op:runBuild is invoked
  then: `stdout` includes the line "from util"
  given: src/hello.ts also imports from "@dxos/echo"
  when: op:buildProject is invoked
  then: the result is `{ ok: false, diagnostics: [{severity: "error", message: <unresolved import>}] }`
        (host externals are deferred to F-13)
```

---

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Scaffold, edit and build a CodeProject
  desc: |
    The core round-trip — create a project, scaffold it, hand-edit a file, build/run it, then
    reset back to empty. `plugin-code` is dev-only: it is enabled by default only in `isDev`
    builds (composer-app's `getDefaults`), off in production.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.3, F-8.1, F-9.1, F-11.1, F-11.2, F-12a]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-code is enabled — dev builds default it on; elsewhere enable it via the plugin
      registry first
    - no CodeProject named "QA Project" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did
      not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the project
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Code Project. Name it "QA Project".
      capture: project
      expect: a CodeProject named "QA Project" appears under the collection, with an empty Spec
        referenced and no source files
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — there is no create operation for CodeProject (F-2.3 is a navtree action);
        this step is human-only.
    - name: Scaffold the project
      do: Ask the assistant (Coder skill) to scaffold the project, or trigger it from the toolbar.
      invoke: [op:scaffoldProject] { project: $project.id }
      capture: scaffolded
      expect: the file tree shows package.json, src/plugin.ts and README.md
      assert: return $result.files.some((f) => f.path === 'src/plugin.ts');
    - name: Write the sanity file
      do: Ask the assistant to run the Hello World sanity check on the project.
      invoke: [op:helloWorld] { project: $project.id }
      expect: src/hello.ts appears in the file tree containing a Hello World program
      assert: return $result.path === 'src/hello.ts';
    - name: Read it back
      do: Click src/hello.ts in the file tree.
      invoke: [op:readFile] { project: $project.id, path: "src/hello.ts" }
      expect: the editor opens src/hello.ts and shows the same content the write produced
      assert: return $result.content.length > 0;
    - name: Build and run it
      do: Click "Run" in the CodeArticle toolbar.
      invoke: [op:runBuild] { project: $project.id }
      expect: the build succeeds with no error diagnostics and stdout shows the program's output
      assert: return $result.ok === true && $result.diagnostics.every((d) => d.severity !== 'error');
  after:
    - name: Reset the project
      do: Ask the assistant to reset the project, or use the "Reset" action in the toolbar.
      invoke: [op:resetProject] { project: $project.id }
      expect: the file tree is empty
      assert: return $result.removed > 0;
    - name: Delete the project
      do: Right-click "QA Project" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$project.id], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Showcase clip
  desc: |
    The 10s showcase clip: Open a new code project. Recorded light at 60 fps with no ident, captions or
    count-in by `tools/autocue/showcase/overnight.mjs`; the clip is the `clip: code` step.
  actors: human
  status: unverified        # driven by autocue/showcase.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-code enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create the object
      do: Create a code object from the + menu.
      expect: it opens in the plank
    - name: Work in it
      do: Click across it as the clip gesture does.
      expect: the object responds to each click
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Specs sync both ways with their files in a local checkout, in the desktop app and in a Composer dev server, through one shared file service; Composer is the spec viewer.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A synced spec references its original location by the key `github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>`. The checkout is found in a predictable place: a list of repositories in settings, or the working directory.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.2, Settings]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: A spec can reference blocks of other specs, and the spec's existing visualizations show those blocks as boxes on the graph.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: An agent skill reviews a spec's compliance and produces a review; the spec viewer annotates the spec with the status from the latest review.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Specs reference code symbols as `github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>#<Symbol>`; double-click or Ctrl-click navigates to the symbol.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15.2, F-15.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The key is stored in the Spec's meta keys as { source: github.com/<owner>/<repo>, id: <path> } and written in text with the `github:` prefix. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14]
  why: plugin-projects and plugin-debug already key imported specs this way, so those specs sync with no migration.
  rejected: A new `source` field on Spec; a single `github:` source string with the repo in the id.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Sync polls every 2 seconds and reconciles three-way against the last agreed text; with no base or on conflict the file wins. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.3]
  why: Polling is one code path for Tauri and the dev route; the repository is where specs are reviewed and versioned, so it wins ties.
  rejected: Tauri's fs watch plus a dev-server websocket (two mechanisms); Composer winning conflicts.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The dev route reads only inside the workspace root and `DX_SPEC_ROOTS`, and writes only `.mdl` files; the desktop app adds no Tauri command and uses the fs plugin's existing scope. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.1, F-14.5]
  why: The route is reachable by any page that can hit localhost, so it is no wider than a spec sync needs.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A source key with a fragment names a spec block or a code symbol by the file's extension; the graph draws both as dashed external boxes, and the Code view shows the file at the symbol inside the spec page. Fills in [D-3] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15]
  why: Showing code beside the spec keeps the spec page the IDE; VS Code is one button away where the host knows the path.
  rejected: Symbol lookup through introspect-mcp, which is node-only and indexes by package rather than by file.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: A review is a `<SPEC>.review.mdl` beside the spec with one `verdict` per item, statuses done, untested, partial, diverged and missing; a feature shows the worst status of its requirements. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16]
  why: An `.mdl` file reuses the parser, syncs through the same file service, and diffs in review like the spec.
  rejected: A JSON sidecar; a section inside the spec, which would make every review a spec change.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Links from a spec to the code that implements it are not part of the spec. They are annotations from another source, rendered as decorations in the editor, the same as the decision chips.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-5
  affects: [SpecArticle, F-15, F-16.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The annotation source is the latest review: each verdict's evidence keys become chips on the item's declaration line and dashed code boxes on the definitions graph, and both open the Code view at the symbol. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.5, F-15.3]
  why: A review already maps each item to its code with checked evidence keys, so no second index is needed and the links stay current with each review.
  rejected: A separate code-map sidecar file; a symbol index built from the code.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Every leaf node is a card or an article, so users meet the same anatomy everywhere (an icon, a menu top right); cards are hosted by one of four containers (masonry, canvas, kanban, list) that share navigation, selection, highlighting, reactivity and scrolling, and each container has a storybook with fixtures. A review verdict is such a card.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-14: A verdict is a VerdictCard (status icon, item id, menu: show in spec, open code) in the list container (Mosaic stack); its stories use the real plugin-file-system review as their fixture. Fills in [D-13].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.4]
  why: The list container already provides keyboard navigation and a current item that can follow the spec; a real review exercises every status.
  rejected: One read-only form per verdict, which gave every verdict three labelled rows and no menu.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Local file access is the `service SpecFs` (read, write, list, roots) with its two backends; the operations that touch local files, op:importSpec and op:listLocalSpecs, sit on top of it and declare `requires: [SpecFs]`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [SpecFs, importSpec, listLocalSpecs, F-14.1]
  why: The code already has one SpecFs with a Tauri and a dev-route backend; a service block states that contract once instead of in each operation.
  rejected: Separate read/write/list operations, which would expose raw file access as agent tools.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Approve [D-15].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-17: A Composer plugin is declared with a `plugin` block (`lang/plugin.mdl`): prose on what it is for and the list of modules it adds. A plugin spec opens with it, directly after the frontmatter; this spec declares `plugin CodePlugin`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodePlugin]
  why: MDL had no plugin ext; the plugin was implied by the document, so its modules could not be described, reviewed or linked to.
  rejected: Capabilities, activation events and requirements per module — left to the code until the dialect grows.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Beside each reviewed item the editor shows one chip row from the review: the status, the code that covers the item (or "no code"), and tested or untested.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.5]
  why: Status, coverage and testing are one judgement about one item; separate rows of chips read as unrelated, and the old chips had low contrast.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: Spec sync uses the generic file-system service in plugin-file-system (github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/PLUGIN.mdl#FileSystem); plugin-code's own `service SpecFs` is removed, op:importSpec and op:listLocalSpecs require the shared service, and its dev route is `/__dx/fs` with extra roots in `DX_FS_ROOTS`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-15
  affects: [importSpec, listLocalSpecs, F-14.1]
  why: File access is not specific to specs; one service serves every plugin and the general-dev direction.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: Reviews judge `scenario` and `test` blocks by whether automation exercises them, citing the test files; the editor marks each as exercised, partly exercised or not exercised, with links to the tests.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.6]
  why: Acceptance scenarios and QA tests were outside the review, so nothing showed whether the behaviour they describe is checked.
```

```mdl
decision D-21: The Coder skill's introspect-mcp server is the built-in DXOS Introspect MCP server, from plugin code with no object in the space and off in a chat by default; the skill no longer declares it, and its instructions tell the agent to turn it on when it needs the tools.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
```

```mdl
decision D-22: Code and test chips show the file name and the declaration on hover. An item with more than one implementation gets a walkthrough of 1 to 5 segments of prose and code, written by the reviewer, shown inline in its Review card and on hover of its status chip. Scenarios and tests read tested, partly tested or not tested.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.6, F-16.7, F-16.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: The spec viewer has a diff mode based on git: on a branch it diffs against the base quickly and detects the branch's pull request; it shows what was added and removed since the base, in the text and in the visualizations.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-17]
```

```mdl
decision D-24: The base is the commit where the branch forked from the pull request's base branch, else the remote's default branch; a second choice diffs against HEAD to show only uncommitted changes. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-17.1]
  why: Diffing against the tip of the base branch would show changes landed there since the fork as reversals on this branch.
```

```mdl
decision D-25: Diff mode marks the definitions graph only, not the data model, API or decision views. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-17.3]
  why: The definitions graph covers every block, so it shows what the other views would.
```

```mdl
decision D-26: Git is reached through new read-only `git` queries on the FileSystem service, answered by the dev route; the desktop app does not offer them yet. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-17.4]
  why: The dev route already runs git, while the desktop app would need a new shell scope for git.
  rejected: Reading `.git` objects directly, which needs packfile and zlib decoding in the page.
```

```mdl
decision D-27: Specs in a GitHub repository that plugin-github syncs as files are mapped by the module SpecFileMapping, with op:importSpecFile and op:exportSpecFile; the mapping is registered at Startup so a sync on EDGE finds it. It sits beside SpecSync, which keeps syncing local checkouts.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [importSpecFile, exportSpecFile]
  why: plugin-github's file sync owns detection, merging and commits, and asks the plugin that owns a format only to import and export it; op:importSpec already names the local-checkout import.
```

```mdl
decision D-28: The `Spec` type is renamed `SpecDocument`, typename `org.dxos.type.specDocument`, with a migration from `org.dxos.type.spec`. Replaces the no-migration rule of F-1.5.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.5, F-1.6, F-2.2, T-1]
  why: `Spec` now names plugin-projects' feature map, which holds at most one SpecDocument as its normative text.
```

```mdl
decision D-29: The spec refers to another spec's item as `<spec id>#<item>`, never by a `github:` key into a `.mdl` file, and declares every spec it refers to as a dependency. A reference names the spec by id ([F-15]).
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-15, F-14.1, importSpec, listLocalSpecs, importSpecFile, SpecArticle]
```

```mdl
decision D-30: plugin-code declares its dependencies with `uses` (it has no runtime plugin dependencies in dx.config.ts): `org.dxos.echo`, `org.dxos.plugin.fileSystem`, `org.dxos.plugin.devShell`, `org.dxos.plugin.github.file-sync` and `org.dxos.spec.review`, each with a one-line reason. The SpecArticle layout mock shows `org.dxos.echo#Database` as its example reference. Fills in [D-29].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-15, F-16, SpecArticle]
  why: Each id is a spec the body already referred to by path or key; the review dialect is named without an item, and ECHO's Database is the example F-15 already used.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: A spec can ask questions; an answered question is recorded as a decision. Every surface that renders a spec shows its questions, drawn with the question component the chat uses. The decisions-by-person view is back in SpecArticle, with the questions at its top.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [SpecArticle, F-18]
```

```mdl
decision D-32: A question is a `question Q-n` block in `## Changelog`, append-only like a decision; it is answered by a later decision with `answers: Q-n`, so "answered" is derived. Fills in [D-31].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-18.3]
  why: Keeping the question unedited keeps the log append-only, and the answer carries the authority of the person who gave it.
  rejected:
    - An `answer:` field written into the question: edits an entry, which the changelog forbids.
```

```mdl
decision D-33: Open questions come before answered ones, and the answering decision is `by:` the current identity's display name with whitespace replaced by `-`, dated today. Fills in [D-31].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-18.1, F-18.3]
  why: Composer knows the person by their identity, not their GitHub username; an open question is the one that needs the reader.
```

```mdl
decision D-34: The decision graph draws questions as cards with an `answers` edge, and a question's `affects:` adds a margin chip that opens the decisions-by-person view. Fills in [D-31].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-18.4]
  why: The graph and the margin are the other places a spec shows its changelog.
```

```mdl
decision D-35: This plugin depends on plugin-projects and renders a spec document only as an article. A spec document embedded as a section, as in a project's Document view, is plugin-projects' plain MDL editor. Supersedes [D-30] where it says the plugin has no runtime plugin dependencies.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:wittjosiah
  why: plugin-projects owns specs and their documents, and a plugin reaches another's UI through surfaces, never its components. This page's margins, diff view and jumps need the editor itself, so it keeps its own.
```

```mdl
decision D-36: The two-way file sync writes a plugin-projects spec's document through its export and reads the file through its import, so the file in the repository keeps its `feat` blocks while the document holds embeds of the feature objects. This page draws the feature cards as well, through a capability plugin-projects contributes.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14, SpecArticle]
```

```mdl
decision D-37: The sync asks each `ProjectCapabilities.SpecDocumentCodec` in turn for a document's file text, passing the text last synced as the base, and copies the text as it is when none answers; a pull goes to the codec that wrote. The page adds every `ProjectCapabilities.SpecDocumentExtensions` contribution to its editor, which rebuilds when they change. Fills in [D-36].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.7, SpecArticle]
  why: The base lets the codec copy what has not changed, so a push touches only the blocks that did. Documents of no plugin keep the copying they had.
```

